<title>JAPAN: Japan hopes for strong, stable euro--Tokyo banker.</title>
<headline>Japan hopes for strong, stable euro--Tokyo banker.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan hopes Europe's single currency will be strong and stable, Yoh Kurosawa, chairman of the Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The greatest concern for Japan is the reliability and stability of the euro, he said. If the euro is unstable, then the dollar/yen exchange rate will inevitably fluctuate greatly, Kurosawa told the Global 24 European economic and monetary union conference.</p>
<p>&quot;If the newly born euro becomes a stable currency, flows of goods and capital between Europe and Japan can be expected to be further activated,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
